            <ArticleTitle>Spinal arachnoid cyst with weakness in the limbs and abdominal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 7-year-old male admitted with neck rigidity, severe pain in the abdomen, and progressive weakness in the lower limbs was diagnosed as having a spinal intramedullary arachnoid cyst. There was a dramatic and immediate recovery after fenestration of the cyst.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
